WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:15.350
Have you ever heard this phrase?

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.900
Sounds good right?

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.653
Quite a proclamation, a call to an epic objective,
an appeal to the people’s pride, towards

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:21.653
resistance.

00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:25.720
The truth, dear folks of VISUALPOLITIK, is
that, over the years, this slogan has become

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.500
one of the chants, the essential slogans of
every protest, especially in Latin America;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.890
And especially in protests and demonstrations
of Marxist, Leninist, Maoist... and socialist

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.640
movements of all kinds.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:48.690
Because, throughout the twentieth century,
these types of chants, proclamations and slogans

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.550
supported a huge number of groups and protest
movements throughout Latin America.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:59.540
To such an extent... that in many cases, these
epic and brave slogans hid a far more terrible

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:00.540
phenomenon.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:05.400
A phenomenon that became one of the most remarkable
characteristics of the entire region: the

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.909
guerrillas.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:16.990
Now, what does the guerrilla phenomenon consist
of?

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.299
Why did it emerge?

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:22.079
How could guerrillas have such an impact,
so much power?

00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:24.200
What’s their situation like today?

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:33.399
We’ll answer all these questions in this
video, but first, a bit of history.

00:01:33.399 --> 00:01:40.069
(THE SPARK THAT IGNITED THE FLAME)

00:01:40.069 --> 00:01:42.429
It’s the 1960s.

00:01:42.429 --> 00:01:44.829
The guerrilla phenomenon is about to begin.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:47.179
The Cuban revolution just happened.

00:01:47.179 --> 00:01:51.490
And folks, we can’t talk about guerrillas
in Latin America... without taking Cuba’s

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:53.649
role into account.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:56.740
Yes, you heard that right.

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:00.969
The Cuban revolution was a great source of
inspiration for all kinds of anti-imperialist,

00:02:00.969 --> 00:02:03.450
revolutionary and communist movements...

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.490
Not only that, but, over the years Cuba also
became the number 1 promoter of guerrilla

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.220
groups in the entire region.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:14.460
Yes, we could say that Cuba was quite a powerful
state in that sense.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:20.170
But the fact is that the myth of the Cuban
revolution was the main reason that thousands

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:25.120
of young idealists, in many cases with good
intentions, helped turn Latin America into

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.340
a hornet's nest.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:30.790
How could they resist the exploits of the
“great commander” Fidel Castro... that

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.010
leader that, supposedly, managed to get the
revolution running with just 82 people.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.189
If he could, why couldn’t others?

00:02:37.189 --> 00:02:38.189
Get the rifles!

00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:42.980
Many of these young people must’ve thought
and felt this quite fevently.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.670
Of course... the actual story was a bit different.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:50.010
See, the truth is that the Revolution managed
to triumph to a great extent, precisely because

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:55.019
of the excessive violence and repression the
Cuban dictator, Fulgencio Batista, committed

00:02:55.019 --> 00:02:56.019
back then.

00:02:56.019 --> 00:03:00.069
Excesses that got a good part of the army,
including several officers, to align with

00:03:00.069 --> 00:03:02.079
Castro’s group.

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:06.719
By the way, did you know that, unlike what’s
commonly said, this heroic revolution didn’t

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.430
actually have a very clear ideological objective?

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:12.629
Yes, you heard that right.

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:18.750
At first, in 1959, Fidel Castro never tired
of repeating, again and again, to the Cuban

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.500
people, among others, that he wasn’t a communist.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.540
Fidel himself said this.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.390
“I know you’re worried about whether or
not we’re communists.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:31.890
I want to make this clear, we aren’t communists,
I’m not a communist, and neither is our

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:32.890
movement.”

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.909
Fidel Castro.)

00:03:35.909 --> 00:03:39.450
We really need to talk about the Cuban revolution
one day, don’t you think?

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:44.670
Folks, many, many of the members of the revolution
were communists; yes, it’s true.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.930
However it wasn’t until 2 years after the
revolutionary triumph, in 1961, that Fidel

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:55.650
declared himself a Marxist-Leninist and proclaimed
the socialist revolution.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:04.290
And here, folks, we can ask ourselves 2 questions.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.099
What changed in these two years?

00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:09.409
And why is this important?

00:04:09.409 --> 00:04:14.269
Listen up.

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:19.130
(OPERATIONS CENTER)

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:20.130
Let's be clear.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:24.260
Washington politicians never believed Fidel
Castro's statements denying communism.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.930
In fact, they saw this new regime in Havana
as a danger during the cold war.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.110
That’s how the disastrous Bay of Pigs invasion
attempt emerged.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:36.080
At the same time, this was quite clear to
the Soviet Union leaders: Cuba meant an incredible

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.060
opportunity, mainly for 3 reasons:

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:45.290
First, by allying with Cuba, they’d gain
a very advantageous geographical position

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.970
with respect to the United States.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.920
They would have friendly territory and a military
base a few kilometers from the American mainland.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:56.510
Second, a socialist Cuba would mean a new
satellite state, thus reinforcing their position

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:57.960
in international politics.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.700
And third, Cuba could become the operation
center to spread communism in the US’s so-called

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:05.540
backyard, that is, in Latin America.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:12.750
That way, folks, the Soviet Union's chances
of winning the Cold War would grow stronger.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:13.920
And, you know what?

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.290
As we usually say here at VISUALPOLITIK, so
it was said and done.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:21.820
The regime, then led by Nikita Khrushchev,
concentrated on consolidating its relations

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.660
with the new Castroite Cuba.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.280
And it was quite a strong focus.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.760
From that very moment, Cuba became a center
for training, financing, and supplying equipment

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.410
and weapons for their revolutionary movements
throughout the continent.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:39.200
That’s how Havana became the biggest guerrilla
uprising promoter in Latin America.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.800
“The duty of every revolutionary is to make
the revolution” The Second Declaration of

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:47.340
Havana, February 4th, 1962.)

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:51.620
The idea, developed by “El Che”, was that
a small group of activists could initiate

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:56.110
typical guerrilla war actions and blow up
existing institutions to spread the flames

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.380
of the socialist revolution.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:02.430
And... not just that, they also promoted a
new strategy known as cultural Marxism...

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.660
Which, by the way, is still seen in many places.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.580
Now, what exactly does this strategy consist
of?

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:12.550
Basically, using education and culture to
help communist and revolutionary ideologies

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:13.860
infiltrate society.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:18.710
To this end, the Cuban regime supported the
creation of songs, poems, university writings

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:22.780
and literary works of all kinds, all with
a common characteristic:

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:27.560
All of them were steeped in revolutionary
ideology and, among other things, extolled

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.560
the guerrilla figure.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:33.590
(“Take education and culture, and the rest
will add on” Antonio Gramsci.)

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:39.870
Now, do you want to know more about how Havana
supported some of the most famous guerrillas?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:45.380
Listen up.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.140
(TIES)

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:51.000
The first operation happened in Nicaragua.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.100
Thanks to Moscow and Havana’s technical,
military and economic support, the revolutionary

00:06:55.100 --> 00:07:00.380
leader, Carlos Fonseca Amador promoted the
creation and organization of the “Sandinista

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.820
National Liberation Front” in 1961.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.510
Ever heard of it?

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:09.980
It’s Daniel Ortega’s movement, the current
tyrant president of Nicaragua, of which we’ve

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:12.580
already spoken in several videos here at VISUALPOLITIK.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.190
But, let's go back to it.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:20.940
In 1969 Carlos Fonseca moved to Havana, where
he spent the next 6 years.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:23.620
From there, he organized the Sandinista front.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:28.780
In 1975 he returned to Nicaragua to solve
some leadership problems and unify the guerrilla

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.780
group.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:34.150
And although a year later this revolutionary
leader was assassinated, in 1979, the Sandinista

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:38.930
Front finally seized power.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:43.490
The guerrilla, trained, financed and supported
by Havana, had triumphed.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.600
The model worked, so why stop?

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:51.570
In 1980, a year after the Sandinista Front’s
triumph, the FMLN “The Farabundo Marti Front

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:56.760
for National Liberation” was founded in
El Salvador with Fidel Castro himself as an

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:57.760
intermediary.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:01.470
And what’s more, this group was founded
in Havana itself.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:04.760
What do you think?

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:09.460
Well, with the support of the Cuban regime,
along with that of the new Nicaraguan government

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:13.970
and Moscow, of course, the FMLN started its
armed fight.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:18.080
Their training centers were located in Cuba
and Nicaragua and, of course, it was those

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:22.940
same countries which provided them with weapons,
supplies, equipment and anything else they

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.570
needed.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:27.180
Now, hold on for a moment.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:30.520
As you can imagine, the United States didn’t
just stand there.

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:36.080
They weren’t willing to give Havana another
victory, so they decided to support the Salvadoran

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.080
government.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.080
The result?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:43.860
12 years of fighting that caused more than
75,000 deaths, thousands of missing people,

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:46.580
and an economic collapse.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:56.060
I think that now we can begin to understand
the magnitude of the violence that has destroyed

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.470
so much of this region.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:01.481
The fact is that on this occasion, folks,
the guerrillas didn’t achieve a revolution

00:09:01.481 --> 00:09:05.490
and after the peace agreements of 1990, they
formed a political party.

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:10.530
Today this party governs El Salvador and,
of course, hasn’t hesitated to support Daniel

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.520
Ortega’s Nicaraguan regime.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:17.280
But... don’t think for a second that this
situation happened solely in Central America,

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.280
not at all.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.560
The southern countries also had their share.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.810
South America also underwent a wave of revolutionary
movements.

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:27.800
In fact throughout Latin America, more than
one hundred-- one hundred--guerrilla groups

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.670
caused enormous damage.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:34.620
Almost all were encouraged and supported by
Cuba in one way or another.

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.931
That’s certainly the case for the 3 most
famous guerrilla groups: The FARC and the

00:09:37.931 --> 00:09:42.860
April 19 Movement in Colombia, and the Shining
Path in Peru.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:48.620
“The Shining Path activists have been trained
in Cuba, Czechoslovakia and the German Democratic

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:49.620
Republic.

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:54.630
Manuel Ulloa, former Prime Minister of Peru
in statements to the El País newspaper in

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:55.630
1983.)

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:59.050
Are you surprised now that the peace agreements
between the FARC and Juan Manuel Santos’

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:01.480
Colombian government will be negotiated in
Havana?

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.540
I mean, why not?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:08.790
Of course, these huge groups, true armies,
also had another fundamental support point:

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:09.790
drug money.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:14.430
Yes, these groups ended up becoming drug traffickers,
a business from which they obtained the enormous

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.380
resources they needed to continue the fight.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:22.170
But, don’t forget, Cuba also went into this
business.

00:10:22.170 --> 00:10:26.050
We told you all about it here on VISUALPOLITIK
in a recent video about Narco-Politics in

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.600
this region of the world.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.820
Yes, the Cuban government even associated
with Pablo Escobar Gavíria himself.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:35.370
And that’s not all… the last example of
Cuban infiltration, which we all know, was

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:41.050
in Venezuela, and we’ve already seen how
things are going there.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:48.490
Folks, Cuba's influence on Latin American
politics in the last 60 years has been terrible.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.310
Havana has played a major role in backing
guerrilla groups and regimes that have done

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.680
no good for Latin America.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.440
Yes, I know, nowadays some people still view
these groups with a certain romanticism...

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.340
that’s a mistake.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:06.510
Beyond the feats and myths, the real story,
unfortunately, was terrible.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:10.920
Fortunately, the guerrillas are now at their
lowest point in decades.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.250
That at least is good news.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.290
By the way, many of the guerrilla groups weren’t
just Havana’s fault.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:21.029
In many cases, they were the fault of a terribly
extractive oligarchy that controlled their

00:11:21.029 --> 00:11:25.510
country with an interest in nothing but maintaining
their own privileges.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:28.700
This has also been one of the great evils
of the region.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:29.700
Just to avoid any confusion, we’ve said
this a thousand times.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:33.630
Folks, with this video, we can now better
understand how so many guerrilla groups suddenly

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:38.529
emerged in Latin America; and why relations
between Washington and Havana have traditionally

00:11:38.529 --> 00:11:39.650
been so bad.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:42.940
The story goes far beyond the missile crisis.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:45.130
So I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did, and don’t forget to

